# MASTER PROMPT — INTERNSHIP APPLICATION HAFUZA

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a complete, functional, responsive, full-stack internship management web application named **"internship application hafuza"**.

This application will be used by multiple students completing their internships at PT One Data Security. It will provide a centralized platform to manage student profiles, internship schedules, digital attendance using dynamic QR codes, daily journals, activity documentation, performance assessments, final internship reports, and announcements.

This must be a real, database-connected application, NOT a static UI prototype, landing page, or frontend-only mockup.

The application must include a working frontend, backend logic, Firebase integration, file storage, authentication, role-based authorization, validation, and a maintainable codebase that can be connected to a new GitHub repository.

### Primary requirements

- Application name: internship application hafuza
- Company: PT One Data Security
- Default language: Bahasa Indonesia
- Secondary language: English
- Platform: Responsive web application for desktop, tablet, and mobile
- Architecture: Full-stack web application
- Authentication: Firebase Authentication with Google Sign-In and email/password
- Database: Cloud Firestore
- File storage: Firebase Cloud Storage
- Source code management: GitHub
- Timezone: Asia/Jakarta
- Internship duration: Configurable start and end dates, typically spanning several months or one semester
- Primary design reference: The provided Spark Admin dashboard screenshot

Use the capabilities available in Google AI Studio Build mode. Create the actual application files, integrate the necessary services, and verify the implementation. Do not merely return a development plan, illustrative code snippets, or a design specification.

If a required external service needs authorization, configuration, billing activation, or manual console setup, clearly identify the exact step instead of pretending that the integration is complete.

